commit 45d77a21
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-22 17:17:03 -0600
subject: feat(usage): generic quota endpoint for custom OpenAI-compatible provider nodes

Add optional usageUrl + usageAuthMode fields to compatible provider nodes
(openai-compatible, anthropic-compatible) and surface them on the quota page:

- open-sse/services/usage/custom.js: generic GET fetcher normalizing common
  quota JSON shapes ({data}, {usage}, flat used/limit, remaining, credits,
  balance, quotas) into the UI row shape {name, used, total, remaining,
  remainingPercentage, resetAt, unlimited}; auth modes bearer/header/none.
- usage.js: dispatch connections with providerSpecificData.usageUrl to the
  generic handler (CUSTOM_USAGE_MARKER) before registry lookup.
- api/usage/[connectionId]: gate now also allows connections whose
  providerSpecificData declares a non-empty usageUrl.
- provider-nodes POST/PUT: accept, validate, persist usageUrl/usageAuthMode;
  PUT propagates to existing connections (clearing works end-to-end).
- providers POST: copy usage fields from node into connection
  providerSpecificData at connection creation.
- ProviderLimits utils.parseQuotaData: default branch now forwards
  remainingPercentage + unlimited so custom nodes render progress bars.
- AddCompatibleModal / EditCompatibleNodeModal: usageUrl + usageAuthMode
  inputs (hidden for multi-compatible).
- tests/unit/custom-usage.test.js: 20 tests covering normalization, auth
  modes, dispatch routing, unlimited, error mapping, parseQuotaData.

Addresses BUG-QUOTA-03 class: custom connections appear on quota page but
fail; now they render when the node declares a usage endpoint.


